// Evolution registry — DATA, not code (ADR-0006/0019/0060). Per-species branch
// evolution conditions: one `SpeciesEvolutions` block per source species, each with
// one or more (trigger -> to_species) branches. Triggers: Level(n) (>= level n),
// Bond(n) (>= bond n; n > 0), Item(id). Every `to_species` is an evolution-only
// DERIVED form and MUST NEVER appear in an encounter table (validate_evolution_fusion).
// Stable ids append-only; no self-evolution; no duplicate source block.
[
    // Flameling (1, wild-obtainable) branch-evolves: to Pyroleo (4) by level, or to
    // Embersworn (5) by bond. The source is a wild species, so the chain is reachable.
    (
        species_id: 1,
        evolutions: [
            (trigger: Level(16), to_species: 4),
            (trigger: Bond(200), to_species: 5),
        ],
    ),
    // ---- pt-d1 playtest roster wave 1 (ADR-0143) -------------------------
    // COMMENT HYGIENE: full-line comments only in this file, and no comment may
    // contain the sequences "species_id:" or "to_species:". The content-integrity
    // eval strips whole-line comments only and then regex-scans the rest, so a
    // trailing comment carrying either would fabricate a phantom evolution block
    // (which surfaces as a bogus self-evolution failure).
    //
    // Cragling (7, Earth) and Shadelet (8, Dark) each get ONE level-triggered
    // branch. Flameling above already demonstrates branch evolution AND the Bond
    // trigger; a bond-gated payoff would make a short playtest non-deterministic.
    // Targets 9 and 10 are evolution-only DERIVED forms — never wild-catchable.
    //
    // MERGE NOTE: this file is a single non-glob file, so a concurrent roster wave
    // also appends here. Keep both stanzas on conflict — nothing else asserts that
    // a given block survives except the pt-d1 gating test.
    (
        species_id: 7,
        evolutions: [
            (trigger: Level(18), to_species: 9),
        ],
    ),
    (
        species_id: 8,
        evolutions: [
            (trigger: Level(20), to_species: 10),
        ],
    ),
]
